        {
          "id": 474722146,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "In this case the ASCII character \\xFF would have to be converted to its UTF-8 representation 0xFFFD (REPLACEMENT CHARACTER) by tvb_get_string_enc() for ENC_ASCII. This should then end up in the PDML (which has UTF-8 encoding as well). But the sample XML file shows here: \\xEF \\xBF \\xBD \\xEF. Not sure where that comes from.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2398962,
            "username": "JaapKeuter",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jaap Keuter",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
