        {
          "id": 474737049,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "When removing the size restriction in the gsnprintf() format string (line 1257: '%.4s' -> '%s') the dissection in Wireshark shows indeed 4 replacement characters for the 4 \\xFF supposed ASCII characters.\n\nNow when you save this as PDML the 4 replacement characters are put in as \\xEF \\xBF \\xBD \\xEF \\xBF \\xBD \\xEF \\xBF \\xBD \\xEF \\xBF \\xBD, which forms a valid UTF-8 sequence of these 4 characters. \n\nSo the solution is to simply remove the format string size in line 1257.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2398962,
            "username": "JaapKeuter",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jaap Keuter",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/722b0c520542a23cb8f8ea7070a45c88f9e9214dc700ac151e419e9649e0304e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/JaapKeuter"
          },
